    "knowledge_point": "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination",
    "problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix.",
    "worked_solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y=8 \\\\  & y=-11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-11$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-11)=8\\,⇒\\,x=8+11=19.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=19$ and $y=-11.$",
